# Keith, 2026-08-16: "that's a private repo, push it all there."
#
# So this is NOT an allowlist. The whole mesh ships — modules, ledgers, state, registries,
# raw node returns, env config. The reason the earlier deny-by-default version existed was a
# near-miss on a PUBLIC repo; keithbbf-gif/bts-mesh is private (confirmed via gh api by the
# QA Engineer, 2026-08-16), and CLAUDE.md canon is explicit that exposure is Keith's call and
# that guarding it is friction, not help.
#
# ⚠ THE ONE THING THAT WOULD MAKE THIS WRONG IS THE REPO GOING PUBLIC. If it is ever flipped,
#   the credentials in gemini_cli_env.json and every balance in the ledgers go with it. That is
#   a property of the REPO, not of this file — so it is recorded here where anyone changing
#   visibility will be standing.

# Only the things that are noise or actively break a checkout:
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.guard.bak
*.lock
.git/
~$*
